WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.473 --> 00:00:03.496
- Over the last five years,
forget about even the election,

00:00:03.496 --> 00:00:07.472
the enormous minority of 
unhappy people in our society

00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:10.325
are dramatically louder 
and are impacting us more

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:14.405
than the far majority of us 
that are happy and good.

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:16.865
There's only so much that 
I can do about being happy

00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:18.875
and documenting 
my happy journey.

00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:20.866
I'm trying to pressure 
the other people

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:22.705
that are happy 
to talk about it too.

00:00:22.705 --> 00:00:24.415
I just think we're in 
a very awkward time.

00:00:24.415 --> 00:00:27.226
I think it's rubbernecking and 
it's just the way it is, right?

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.375
We pay more attention to 
the negative than the positive.

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:31.645
It's just how I feel 
about the world.

00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:34.155
I think human beings are the

00:00:34.155 --> 00:00:35.415
most underrated 
thing of all time.

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:36.455
When I think about our

00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:39.055
capabilities to 
eliminate each other,

00:00:39.055 --> 00:00:41.287
I'm being serious, I know 
it's a kinda weird place to go,

00:00:41.287 --> 00:00:42.937
but the fact 
that we're still here

00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:45.026
we are hard-wired 
in a way that allows us

00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:47.666
to protect each 
other in a net game

00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:50.085
yet the mainstream media 
and the way we hear

00:00:50.085 --> 00:00:52.007
all you hear is negativity.

00:00:52.007 --> 00:00:54.375
All that mainstream media 
does is tell us about the

00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:59.026
.0001% worst of us.

00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:00.237
I think we as humans

00:01:00.237 --> 00:01:03.506
are going to have some level 
of a sense of responsibility

00:01:03.506 --> 00:01:06.275
that if you're in a good 
place it might be good to

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:10.387
tweet or Instagram or 
Snapchat about that versus

00:01:10.387 --> 00:01:12.805
what we default into 
which is there are people's

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.777
Twitter feeds that are basically
every seven or ten days

00:01:15.777 --> 00:01:17.817
when they're 
complaining about an airline

00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:20.127
or venting about work.

00:01:20.127 --> 00:01:23.427
The volume of negativity 
is just way too high

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:27.387
in reality of what's going on
and I think the silent majority

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:30.886
of us, and this is what happens,
every empire falls when the

00:01:30.886 --> 00:01:33.947
silent majority of 
happy isn't loud enough.

00:01:33.947 --> 00:01:36.167
(somber music)

